lifeos-nix patch f-derived-watch-wire — wire DerivedWatch into Pulse loadModules

PROBLEM
  DerivedSync (regenerates PRINCIPAL_TELOS / LIFEOS_STATE / Data-Plane on USER edits) has no
  Linux on-change trigger — upstream ships only launchd WatchPaths (macOS). Without it derived
  artifacts refresh only on the daily cron / install_core, so a mid-day TELOS edit leaves the
  @-imported PRINCIPAL_TELOS stale until 03:30.

FIX
  Ship a DerivedWatch module (LIFEOS/PULSE/modules/derived-watch.ts, added in installPhase 1b)
  and wire it into pulse.ts loadModules: inotify (fs.watch) on the USER source subtrees +
  debounce + single-flight, inside the Pulse process (no extra daemon, no polling). Default-on
  (config.derived_watch.enabled !== false); the daily derived-sync cron stays as safety-net.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One hunk in pulse.ts loadModules (import + start, mirrors the existing module pattern). The
  module file is added separately in installPhase. Disjoint from f-telos-source and f4-*.

VERIFICATION
  Standalone test (dev box): an edit-burst coalesces into ONE DerivedSync run (debounce), a
  later edit re-fires, and output writes (PRINCIPAL_TELOS/LIFEOS_STATE) are ignored — no
  self-trigger loop. Post-build: module present in payload; Pulse boots and logs
  "[derived-watch] watching N USER dirs". Hunk via `diff -u`, never hand-counted.

